  "fallback_policy":{
    "json_failure":"skip optional dataset and continue with canonical datasets",
    "country_failure":"use the canonical country record in data/countries/",
    "empty_description":"show record identity plus available relationships and evidence rather than a blank page"
  },
  "integrity_requirements":[
    "Public Room definitions resolve through data/atlas-views.json rather than a fixed door count",
    "Legacy Tim, Religion, Philosophy, Science and World URLs remain compatibility projections while migration is active",
    "World Map, Politics, North and World Systems remain specialist sibling or nested Views over canonical backend owners",
    "Every major manifest branch has an explicit primary_view, global_route or backend_only projection state",
    "Canonical ownership remains in source/canonical records; this bridge owns routing intent only",
    "Atlas Node IDs and routes remain stable while Views may evolve independently",
    "Every relationship endpoint resolves or is explicitly marked unresolved",
    "Unknown data is represented as missing/unknown, never as zero",
    "Backend-only or research-heavy records remain discoverable without becoming homepage clutter",
    "Requested record paths are fetched only after resolving through an approved registry/manifest allowlist"
  ],
  "design_rule":"Configurable Atlas Views above, canonical Nodes on the Plane, recoverable Archive depth below. Compatibility routes may remain while ownership and discovery migrate, but no fixed public-door count defines the House."
